.TH FFF 1 "2026-06-06" "0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fff \- Fucking Fast File Manager (Crystal port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fff
[\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
fff is a blazingly fast terminal file manager written in Crystal. It provides a keyboard-driven interface for navigating and managing files with minimal overhead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B DIRECTORY
Start fff in the specified directory instead of the current working directory.
.TP
.B \-p
Run as a file picker (writes selected file path to ~/.cache/fff/opened_file).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help information.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
All keybindings are configurable via FFF_KEY_* environment variables. Defaults listed below.
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B j, \fB↓\fR
Scroll down
.TP
.B k, \fB↑\fR
Scroll up
.TP
.B h, \fB←\fR
Go to parent directory
.TP
.B l, \fB→\fR
Enter directory / open file
.TP
.B g
Go to top
.TP
.B G
Go to bottom
.TP
.B PgUp
Scroll up one screenful
.TP
.B PgDn
Scroll down one screenful
.TP
.B -
Go to previous directory
.TP
.B ~
Go to home directory
.TP
.B :
Go to directory (type path)
.TP
.B t
Go to trash directory
.TP
.B e
Refresh current directory
.TP
.B .
Toggle hidden files visibility
.SS File Operations
.TP
.B SPACE
Mark / unmark file
.TP
.B m
Mark all files
.TP
.B y
Yank (copy) marked files to clipboard
.TP
.B v
Cut (move) marked files to clipboard
.TP
.B p
Paste files from clipboard to current directory
.TP
.B d
Delete marked files (move to trash)
.TP
.B S
Create symbolic link
.SS File Management
.TP
.B r
Rename file under cursor
.TP
.B b
Bulk rename marked files (opens $EDITOR)
.TP
.B n
Create new directory
.TP
.B f
Create new file
.TP
.B x
Show file attributes (permissions, size, mtime)
.TP
.B X
Toggle executable permission
.SS Preview & Search
.TP
.B i
Preview file content (bat -> less -> builtin)
.TP
.B /
Search files (navigable fuzzy search)
.TP
.B !\fIquery\fR
Content search via ripgrep (prefix with ! in search mode)
.SS Miscellaneous
.TP
.B s
Spawn shell in current directory
.TP
.B =
Cycle sort mode (name -> size -> time)
.TP
.B +
Reverse sort order
.TP
.B 1-9
Jump to favorite directory
.TP
.B q
Quit fff
.SH CONFIGURATION
fff reads configuration from environment variables and ~/.config/fff/config.json.
Environment variables take precedence over JSON.
.SS Core Options
.TP
.B EDITOR
Text editor for bulk rename (default: vi)
.TP
.B FFF_OPENER
File opener command (default: xdg-open on Linux, open on macOS)
.TP
.B FFF_TRASH
Trash directory path (default: ~/.local/share/fff/trash)
.TP
.B FFF_CD_ON_EXIT
Enable saving current directory on exit (0 or 1)
.TP
.B FFF_CD_FILE
Path to the cd-on-exit helper file (default: ~/.cache/fff/.fff_d)
.SS Favorite Directories
.TP
.B FFF_FAV1 \- FFF_FAV9
Favorite directories accessible via keys 1-9
.SS Key Bindings (all optional, defaults shown)
All keys can be rebound via FFF_KEY_<ACTION>.
.TP
Available actions:
UP, DOWN, ENTER, QUIT, SEARCH, PARENT, MARK, MARK_ALL, COPY, MOVE, PASTE, DELETE, NEW_DIR, MKFILE, RENAME, BULK_RENAME, PREVIEW, SHELL, HIDDEN, HOME, PREVIOUS, REFRESH, ATTRIBUTES, EXECUTABLE, GO_DIR, GO_TRASH, SYMLINK, TOP, BOTTOM, PAGE_UP, PAGE_DOWN.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/fff/.fff_d
CD on exit helper file
.TP
.I ~/.cache/fff/opened_file
Picker mode output (written with -p flag)
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/fff/trash/
Default trash directory
.TP
.I ~/.config/fff/config.json
JSON configuration file
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start fff in the current directory:
.B fff
.TP
Start fff in a specific directory:
.B fff /home/user/documents
.TP
Use as file picker in vim:
.B fff \-p
.TP
Configure custom trash directory:
.B export FFF_TRASH="$HOME/.local/share/fff/trash"
